":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Originally reported by: **the mulhern (BitBucket: [the_mulhern](http://bitbucket.org/the_mulhern))**\n\n---\n\nHere's a little mini-example:\n\n```\n#!python\n\nclass Junk(object):\n\n    def __init__(self, priority, *args, **kwargs):\n        self._setPriority(priority)\n\n    def _setPriority(self, p):\n        self._priority = p\n\n    priority = property(_setPriority,\n                        doc=\"The priority of the swap device\")\n```\n\nPylint complains\n\n Attribute '_priority' defined outside __init__ (attribute-defined-outside-init)\n\nIt depends on what you mean by outside, since self._priority is defined during execution of \n\n```\n#!python\n\n__init__\n```\n\n.\n\nI don't think that pylint analyses can make call graphs, so I do not expect that W0201 analysis will be able to detect this, or to detect similar idioms that use, e.g., properties, like:\n\n```\n#!python\n\nclass Junk(object):\n\n    def __init__(self, priority, *args, **kwargs):\n        self.priority = priority\n\n    def _setPriority(self, p):\n        self._priority = p\n\n    priority = property(_setPriority,\n                        doc=\"The priority of the swap device\")\n```\n\nBut maybe message should be something like:\n\n\"Attribute '<attribute>' not assigned to in body of **init**\"\n\nor something like that.\n\n---\n- Bitbucket: https://bitbucket.org/logilab/pylint/issue/192\n","closed_by":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://a